PATCH 121 -- MAINMENU version-string glyph blitter: recover the c684 entry (0x19ae) + fix the
per-glyph blit (FUN_0000_19ea) base-losses.

The bottom-of-screen version string "AF-FD 1U10" is drawn glyph-by-glyph by 5591 via the driver text
vector c684 (= MGAVIDEO seg:0x19ae).  0x19ae is a mid-function entry Ghidra folded into FUN_0000_198e,
so it was absent from the driver fmap and the c684 dispatch reached nothing -> no version string.
And the glyph blit itself, FUN_0000_19ea, was decompiled with its font segment [0x71a], framebuffer
segment [bx] (=[0x736][0]), text-state struct base [0x736] and rowtable all base-lost, plus the
8-bits/row plot idiom (`add ah,ah; je; inc di; adc cx,cx; sub di,cx; rep stos`) mangled into a wrong
span loop -> it would have drawn garbage even if reached.

Fix: reconstruct 0x19ae (the wrapper: fb-check -> 2d6d transform + rowtable setup + 19ea + 2e12) and
register it in the fmap so c684 resolves; reconstruct 19ea instruction-faithfully from the asm
(0x19ea..0x1b5c) -- 1-bpp glyph bitmap (byte0 = blank flag, then one byte per row, MSB-first, set
bits get the colour) drawn at rowtab[cursor.row]+cursor.col in the framebuffer segment, then the
cursor-advance and the control-character (bs/lf/cr/ff/...) sub-cases.  asm-verified: 0x19ae, 0x19ea.
